# The two env vars this app needs to boot against the local Supabase stack
# (supabase/config.toml). Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored, per
# `.env*` in .gitignore) and fill in real values before running `npm run
# dev` or the test suite.
#
# Whole-branch review Finding I1 (2026-09-07 fix wave): these were
# previously documented in no tracked file — `supabase/.env.example`
# covers only the SERVER-side `SUPABASE_AUTH_*` variables (Google OAuth,
# Twilio), not these two CLIENT-side `VITE_` ones. Without them, `getClient()`
# (src/session/supabase.ts) throws `supabaseUrl is required.`, and a plain
# `git clone && npm install && npm run dev` gave a blank page with no
# diagnostic. `onAuthChange` (src/session/auth.ts) now fails soft — a
# missing/misconfigured value degrades the app to signed-out, local-only
# rather than crashing — but this file is the actual fix for "no diagnostic":
# it exists so a fresh clone has something to copy and fill in.
#
# Values below are the Supabase CLI's own well-known local-dev demo
# constants (the same ones already sitting in this worktree's `.env.local`,
# per that file's own comment) — safe to commit as an EXAMPLE, but never
# commit the real `.env.local` itself regardless.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54331
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0
